Sweep's kit now draws and behaves the way you described, and v0.1.28 is live on Pages.

**What changed**
- **Brooms are real characters now.** One shared shape: a binder row `/=====\` over three dense `|||||||` rows, cached per size and stretched to span the head. Melee, thrown broom, split brooms and the heavy all use it; the old shaft-plus-fan polygon is gone.
- **Melee:** upright head in front of the avatar, bristles always at the bottom, and it strokes straight up and down across the lane instead of riding the arc. Hit one strokes down, hit two back up, the big third hit spans the whole lane.
- **Heavy:** generated in front of the player (`powerFront` 110), then one big stroke up (`powerRise` 281) and back down the same lane in 0.9 s, carrying bodies with it. Width is 80% of the view, and the stroke direction sets the shove, so victims are pushed up on the rise and back down on the return instead of being dragged toward you. Cover still cuts contact.
- **Firing:** `fireBroomSweep` no longer re-checks energy after the charge (the charge start already gated it), and a release on the completion tick fires instead of cancelling. That was the "gets ready, never fires" path.
- **Core mark:** back to `✷`. The two-row broom picture was tested in the core and turned to mush at ~11 px, so the star stays and the kit carries the broom.

**Verified**
- `npx tsc --noEmit` clean; `npm run build` clean.
- Headless sim run: heavy fires, deals 2, carries the target up then down, leaves a body outside the lane untouched; split-broom skill still damages and shoves.
- `npm run bench`: 8P max proj 0.085 ms avg / 0.244 p99, gauntlet 0.228 / 0.779 — inside budget.
- Visual pass in the dev arena on the melee pose, heavy mid-stroke and the star core.
- Pages run 40997991085 succeeded; production is serving the build hash I compiled (`index-3C-xjlWi.js`).

One caveat: the live keyboard/gamepad hold path couldn't be automated in the browser (synthetic key holds get dropped when the tab loses focus), so the "never fires" fix is covered by the sim test and the code path rather than a recorded controller press. That's the first thing worth checking on your side: hold power as Sweep and confirm the stroke fires even if you release exactly as it fills.

The docs are updated to match: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) D14 now records the character-drawn brooms, upright melee stroke and the two-way heavy, and [HISTORY.md](HISTORY.md) has the pass-2 entry with the numbers.

