Production now has all of it: **v0.1.30 is live** at https://spuds0588.github.io/DEFLECT/, serving the same bundle I built locally (`index-wqKMDC3i.js`).

**Identity no longer depends on mode**
The bug was that VS BOTS runs `World('match')` under the hood, and the renderer used `mode === 'match'` to choose slot colours and slot glyphs. That one check is now an `online` flag, so every local mode draws program colour, hull and glyph. Only a networked guest falls back to slot identity, because the snapshot still does not carry programs. Score pips follow the same rule.

**Bots are player characters now**
Local bots draw the same program hull as the avatar, with real three-segment health (lost segments ghost, current health lights), the same multi-pass glow, and the core shrinking with their damage. They keep no heading arrow, energy arc or readiness dock. A one-health Probe bot now reads as one lit arc and two ghosts, not a bare ring.

**Toxic.exe**
- Green six-point star hull, `☠` core. The star needed a real segment trim (half an edge) before the three health pieces read at full health.
- Ranged: a `†` needle (type 7), light direct damage plus venom. No bounce, no motion tail.
- Venom: 3.5 s, a tick every 0.75 s. Poisoned bodies get a pulsing green rim and a flashing `☠`.
- Skill: 360° burst that damages and poisons through clear line of sight, drawn as a steady spray of neon circles for the whole 0.7 s, the death-shard burst made round and green.
- Power: a rooted, aimable jet. 0.8 s charge, 1.25 s stream, damage ticks every 0.2 s, cover cuts both the drawn shaft and the damage. The stick still steers at 2.4 rad/s while the body is locked.
- Bots tap the spray at close range; the generic heavy hold builds the jet.

![Program select](screenshots/toxic-select.png)
![Venom jet](screenshots/toxic-jet7.png)
![Spray burst](screenshots/toxic-burst4.png)
![Bot hull](screenshots/bot-hull.png)

**Verified**
- `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` clean.
- Headless: needle applies venom, spray hits and poisons in radius, jet fires after charge, moves 0 units while rooted, turns at the capped rate, ticks damage, and does nothing through a pillar.
- Browser at 1920×1080: five program cards, green star in training and VS BOTS, bot hull with lit and ghost segments, jet stopping at cover, circle spray.
- `npm run bench`: 8P max projectiles 0.081 ms avg / 0.220 p99; gauntlet 0.197 / 0.701. Inside budget.
- Pages run `41005250308` succeeded; production returns HTTP 200 and contains `TOXIC.EXE`.

Two things worth knowing before you test: gauntlet worms, viruses, sentries and error blocks take spray/jet damage but cannot be poisoned yet, and the jet has no charge tell in the arena. Both are listed in [TODO.md](TODO.md). Docs are current in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) (D4 revised, D15 added) and [HISTORY.md](HISTORY.md).

The first thing to judge is the jet's feel: whether 2.4 rad/s lets you track a moving target without feeling like a turret, and whether 1.25 s is long enough to matter.
