![Program select](screenshots/kaboom-prod.png)

**The kit**
- **Ranged**: a slow shell (250 u/s) that does no direct-hit damage. It detonates on a body, on cover, or at the end of its fuse for a 52-radius blast, 1 damage and a 520 shove. Cover cuts the blast, so a shell landing behind a pillar clears nothing.
- **Skill**: a heavy shell lobbed 300 units in a 0.62 s arc. It flies over pillars, lands, and detonates for 2 damage in a 116 blast; it also blows up on the first body it meets.
- **Power**: five lobbed shells in a shallow fan, released as the string above. Each has a 66 blast and 1 damage; overlapping blasts are intended to make the rough rectangle.
- **Identity**: red-orange square made of four inward triangles, three health segments and one frame-only triangle, with the bomb mark at the core. Bots use the same kit: they lob at 90 to `lobRange + 60`, and the generic heavy hold builds the carpet.

![Shell in flight and blast](screenshots/kaboom-bomb4.png)

**One thing about the bomb symbol**: this machine does not have Wingdings installed, so `document.fonts.check` claims the font exists and the core rendered a literal red letter `M`. I fixed the detection to compare glyph advances against a missing family, so this host draws a vector bomb instead, while a machine with Wingdings still gets the `M` glyph. The core and every shell use the same mark.

