![Campaign drill with the bot squad](screenshots/campaign-drill-prod-fight.png)

**BUILD ROOT (campaign node 1)** — shipped in v0.1.34, now tuned:

- 18 s **sparring drill** against the run's bot squad, then a 3.4 s **SYSTEM BREACH** warning, then the threat assault. Your squad de-rezzes on the breach and the room belongs to the hostiles.
- The drill squad now forms an arc 250 units *in front of you* and respawns on that arc, so the spar starts immediately. Before this they used the arena's spawn ring, which on CROSSROADS meant a five-second jog before anyone engaged. You also keep the gauntlet spawn, so a drill knockdown puts you back in the fight instead of across the map.
- The assault opens with a sentry pack, adds worms, then a new pack every 14 s. Delete 10 threats to clear. One death fails the node — the failure overlay and RETRY/SLOTS path work.
- Clearing writes the save slot (node, program, players, bots, seconds) and returns to the slot list; a filled slot resumes.

**Camera framing**

The follow camera is no longer a strict player-follow. Live bodies near you — other players, the training drone, worms, viruses, sentries, error blocks — pull the frame toward the group. The pull is a distance-weighted mean, capped at half the offset, so a threat behind you opens the view while a brawl on every side cancels out. Your avatar is then clamped to the middle band of the view, so the pull can never push you off-screen; arena walls still win when you're in a corner. Numbers live in the new `CAMERA` block in [config.ts](src/game/config.ts), and the reasoning is recorded in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

**Verified**

- Headless: drill squad 250 units and clear of cover on all six arenas at 1–3 bots; timeline drill 18.0 s → breach 21.4 s → assault; a fighting player reaches 10 kills and clears; an idle player fails.
- Browser: drill with both bots engaged, wave/breach banners, and a staged sentry 350 units out pulled the camera so the player sat at 0.39 of the view and the sentry at 0.90 (no pull would have left the sentry off-screen).
- `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run build`, `npm run bench` (sim unchanged: 0.094 ms max-proj avg, 0.208 ms gauntlet) clean. Pages deployed successfully; production serves **v0.1.35 IN TESTING**.

**What I want feedback on:** whether 18 s of drill is the right length before the breach; whether the camera pull feels natural in 1v1 and 1v3 (it's tuned to be a lean, not a swing); the assault's opening pressure — an idle player dies in under 10 seconds, so it may need a softer first pack; and whether the drill bots should focus only on you (right now they're free-for-all and will trade hits with each other).

Two known limits: only one node is authored, so a cleared slot replays BUILD ROOT, and bots are drill-only — they can't fight beside you after the breach until `World` has a team model. Dynamic camera zoom stays deferred because the Sweep heavy and sentry pack window are built on the fixed zoom.
