{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p83-7987a173","text":"The user wants:
1. A map called "RECYCLING BIN" (they wrote "recyling bin") with no walls on the outside and a big square hole in the middle.
2. Environmental pushers that periodically push everything in the map down rapidly, so it falls into the hole or lands on one of the sides of the hole.
3. Holes and gaps should be able to be jumped by dashing across them.

Also I was mid-verification of the fall on prod — let me first finish that check, then implement.

Note on #3: "holes and gaps should be able to be jumped by dashing across them." Currently chasms are body-blockers and dash phases solids (`if (p.dashT <= 0)` for cover collision) — so dash already phases through chasms? Wait: `stepPlayerMotion` takes `solids` = pillars + chasms and skips collision when `dashT > 0`. So a dash already crosses a trench. D8 says "A dodge still phases solids, so a charged dash can cross a trench." So that already works.

But for a "hole" in the middle — should it be a chasm (body blocker) or a fall hazard? The user's "big square hole in the middle" is a *fall* hazard, not a blocker — you can be pushed into it, and it's a hole, so bodies that enter it fall. Hmm, but existing chasms are body-blockers (like a trench you can't enter, only cross by bridge/pad/lift). The new mechanic should be: an interior hole you can fall into (and dash across).

The user's instruction: "give it no walls on the outside and a big square hole in the middle" + "pushers that periodically push everything down so it falls in the hole or lands on one of the sides of the hole" + "holes and gaps should be able to be jumped by dashing across them".

So: interiors holes should be fall hazards: walking into one = fall; a dash crosses it. That's distinct from the trench blocker. So I need a new arena field, e.g. `voids: Rect[]` (fall holes) in ArenaDef, separate from `traverse.chasms`.

