Everything landed and is live on the main-branch deploy: **v0.1.39 [IN TESTING]** at <https://spuds0588.github.io/DEFLECT/>.

## Compaction arm

- **30 s cycle**: 2.6 s warning, a **98 u/s stroke** (well under a player's 248), then a slow 5 s climb back. It's 130 units thick, hatched like steel, and narrows with the arena as it descends, so it reads as a moving wall rather than a sweep line.
- It **stops exactly on the hole's leading edge** (y 786), not at the floor lip. Bodies are glued to its face and carried at the plate's speed: anything over the hole drops in, anything on the left/right ledges gets pinned at the bottom and survives. The safe floor visibly shrinks over the stroke, then reopens.
- **No solid cover in the bin any more.** Pillars would pin bodies in front of the plate instead of pushing them. Only breakable boxes are in there.
- The arena is a **trapezoid** (430-unit inset at the top, full width at the bottom) with a big bottom hole (695→1295 wide) and the two side ledges as the only safe ground under the arm.

## Fall grace

Crossing a lip, slant or hole edge no longer kills on that frame. A **0.6 s grace** starts: the body hangs over the drop, still steers at 62% speed against a 74 u/s outward pull, and is **saved if it gets back on the floor**. Death still runs the ordinary `SRC.VOID` path if the timer expires. Headless checks: no input dies at 0.6 s, steering back saves.

## File boxes

Light debris, not furniture: rounded **dashed** outlines, no overlap (they shove each other apart), a body running into one launches it, a lash **launches without deleting** (still 2 hp, so the second hit breaks it), a raised guard bats it, shots and blasts shove it, and the arm sweeps it into the pit. Motion uses a target velocity with a fast ramp and low drag, so a shove eases in and coasts. New boxes drop back in during the quiet window.

## Solid boundaries

Walled arenas now have a wide bleed, a thick solid rim and a bright white inner face; cover pillars get a glow band plus a hard rim and inner line. Open lips and trapezoid edges stay dashed, so "drop" and "wall" no longer look alike.

## Wedge's wall

It's solid to every shot type and has **7 hp**: shots chip 1, spears/brooms/bombs chip 2, a lash chips 1, blasts chip 2. It shakes on hits, shows **three crack stages**, and de-rezzes with its own break burst at zero. The one deliberate exception is the lobbed shell, which is airborne; the charged laser is still a piercing heavy and isn't stopped by the plate. That's a design call I documented rather than changed.

## Campaign score

`BUILD ROOT` now authors **six data crates**, spawned on the breach so the drill squad can't break them. The clear reports kills, time, damage taken, data preserved and a score (kills + data + time vs par − damage), with a **1500-point clean-sweep bonus** for keeping every crate. Best score and clean-sweep count persist in the save slot. Result overlays also hold **1.1 s** now so you see the aftermath before the buttons appear.

## Checks

`tsc --noEmit` clean, `npm run build` clean, bench unchanged (gauntlet 0.226 ms avg), headless checks for the arm (mid-arena body dies at the rim, side bodies pinned alive), fall recovery, wall hp 7→0 and blocking every shot, and the campaign crates. Browser pass on the dev build and on production for the trapezoid, plate, props and the bolder walls. No console errors.

**Known gaps:** destructible *cover* (pillars) isn't built yet — it needs a data record before a map asks for it; file boxes stay local-only until the snapshot can carry them.

If you want to tune this next, the natural knobs are the arm's stroke speed (98 now) and the box shove distance.
