The attract demo, the UI toggle and the bot fixes are all in **v0.1.46**.

## Title attract demo

Leave the hub alone for 24 seconds and it hands the screen to a bot-run gauntlet: a random program, a random arena, no canvas UI, and a HARD `BotBrain` playing through the camera. Any key, click, wheel or gamepad press brings the title back on the next frame. Hover does not count as input, because a layout change can fire a synthetic `pointermove` under a resting cursor and that was cutting the demo off instantly.

- `?attract=1` boots it immediately for QA.
- Death restarts into a fresh random run after 4 seconds.
- It never writes a gauntlet record, never opens an overlay, and never touches the save slots.

## Way more enemies

The demo now opens at wave **72** with the room filled to its live caps: **5 sentries, 2 worms, 10 viruses and 12–14 error blocks**, instead of one pack. A demo-only top-up runs every 5 seconds (`ATTRACT.refill`) so the fight does not thin out between the normal wave timers. It reuses the ordinary spawn paths, so assembly, sound and the threat simulation are unchanged. Verified on CROSSROADS, TRANSIT and THE RING.

## Game UI setting

Settings > Feedback now has **GAME UI**, and `?ui=0` does the same for one load without saving the preference. It hides the match strip, wave banners, readiness docks and minimap; the avatar's own health segments and lock reticle stay, because those are gameplay marks rather than UI.

The readiness dock was rebuilt around five identical **34 px circular slots**: bigger ammo dots, bigger dash chevrons, skill and heavy marks scaled up about 30%, and cooldowns drawn as a circular mask with a lit sweep edge instead of a faint arc. The panel is still 182×44, so the boxes did not grow.

## Bot jitter and the shield

The jitter was exactly what you suspected: bots could not use target lock, so every shot meant stepping straight at the target and every spacing correction pulled them back. They now **hold target lock while fighting**, which keeps facing on the target and lets them strafe and shoot at the same time. Spacing is continuous (approach far, orbit at the hold range, back off only when crowded) instead of hard thresholds, the A* route is committed for half a second once cover breaks the line, and the near-field cover probe no longer fights the route and pins the bot against a pillar.

They also raise the **180° guard** on incoming bolts outside melee reach, turn to face the bolt while the shield arms, and keep the dodge and Wedge wall in the mix.

## Overcharge beam

Found it: `drawLasers` always `continue`d out of the heavy-charge branch, so a live beam was skipped whenever the charge ring was also drawing. It now falls through and draws the beam. The gauntlet pilot also holds the overcharge beam for a short burst and strafes the line across the target, instead of tapping it for one frame where it was invisible.

## Checks

`npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` are clean. Headless: match movement reversals dropped **18 → 5 in 12 s**, gauntlet **2 in 12 s**; the bot closes on a distant target and the round resolves; a 25 s mirror match held guard 104 frames and had it up 228 frames. Browser: `?attract=1` reports 5 sentries / 2 worms / 10 viruses / 14 blocks with `showUi` false, the idle path started on its own at 24 s, and a pointerdown returned to the title and restored the saved UI. I could not capture a screenshot because the preview tab is not currently being drawn.

Everything is live at <http://127.0.0.1:5179> as 0.1.46 and remains uncommitted.

If you want the demo to read more like a highlight reel, the next pass would tune how long it survives and how dramatically the camera follows the action.
