Tuning now has one home, and it is live in production.

## The split

Gameplay values live in five JSON records under [src/game/tuning](src/game/tuning):

- [player.json](src/game/tuning/player.json) — avatar movement, health, energy, dash, melee, guard, lock, heavy beam, `BOLT`, `BUG`, `MINE`.
- [programs.json](src/game/tuning/programs.json) — the six kits: `WEDGE`, `FISHER`, `SWEEP`, `TOXIC`, `KABOOM`, `BUFFER`.
- [threats.json](src/game/tuning/threats.json) — gauntlet wave pacing and every hostile family.
- [campaign.json](src/game/tuning/campaign.json) — the authored node's drill/breach pacing and score weights.
- [world.json](src/game/tuning/world.json) — camera, fall, file boxes, traversal, powerups, rounds, training, net and the attract demo.

[config.ts](src/game/config.ts) is now a typed facade. It imports those records, re-exports every old name, and adds only the values that must stay derived: the two `PI/2` sector half-angles and Sweep's `powerRise`/`powerSpan`, which scale with the view. Engine limits, view size, pool sizes, `TRAVEL`, `TRAIL_LEN` and the render palette stay in code because they are not feel knobs.

No system changed: nothing imports JSON directly. Editing a number is a JSON edit; a running dev server hot-reloads it, and production picks it up on the next build. There is deliberately no runtime config fetch, so snapshots, bot determinism and the PWA cache are untouched.

## Verification

- A temporary deep-compare script imported the previous `config.ts` from `HEAD` and the new facade, then compared **all 40 exports recursively**: **identical**, no key or value changes. The four derived fields were recomputed with the same formulas.
- `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` are clean.
- Browser: the attract demo still starts at wave 72 with sentries, worms, viruses and error blocks live, and the console reports build 0.1.47 with no errors.
- [tuning/README.md](src/game/tuning/README.md) documents the file map, units, derived fields and the invariants easiest to break while tuning; AGENTS.md now records this as D24.

