Sweep's heavy now assembles as a directional pass, and the bodies in the lane get moved before anyone takes a hit.

## What changed

- **Reveal, then stroke.** Firing the heavy now runs a 0.3 s materialize beat before the rise/fall. The broom stays at the cast point and fills in from one side; only after the whole head is present does the damaging stroke begin. Cooldown still starts when the stroke ends.
- **Direction follows facing.** Facing left of the lane centre (`cos(facing) < -0.15`) reveals **right to left**; everything else reveals **left to right**. The direction is latched on the fire frame, so steering during the charge can't flip it mid-materialize.
- **The reveal is a shove, not a hit.** Bodies under the part of the lane that is already visible are pushed toward the growing front with `SWEEP.powerRevealPush` (820) and take **zero damage**. That includes other players, sentries, viruses and worms; cover cuts the shove through the same line test as the stroke. Once the head is fully on the lane, the normal per-body damage and carry rules run unchanged.
- **Readable charge.** The charge now shows a faint full-width ghost of the lane instead of blooming a bright head from the middle. On commit, the same bright head reveals from the facing side with a bright front edge riding the cut, so the materialize doesn't pop in at full width.

All numbers are in [programs.json](src/game/tuning/programs.json) under `SWEEP`: `powerRevealTime` (0.3 s) and `powerRevealPush` (820) are the two to tune if it feels slow or the shove too weak. The implementation is in [world.ts](src/game/world.ts), [render.ts](src/game/render.ts) and [types.ts](src/game/types.ts); [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) D10/D14 and [HISTORY.md](HISTORY.md) are updated, and the build is stamped **v0.1.48**.

## Checks

- `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` are clean.
- Headless, full charge-to-fire input: facing right fires at tick 36 with `broRevealDir=1`, a body on the early part of the lane takes no damage through the reveal (`hp` stays 3), then is hit on the first stroke tick. Facing left gives `broRevealDir=-1` and a negative shove.
- Gauntlet sentry: hp unchanged during the reveal, pushed from x=430 to x=471, then killed by the stroke. Same for a worm (`kx=730`).
- I could **not** capture a screenshot: the preview tab has not been drawn because the Freebuff window is minimized/covered, so visual confirmation of the bright front is still yours to make at <http://127.0.0.1:5179>.

Everything is live on the dev server as 0.1.48 and remains uncommitted, along with the pre-existing untracked `screenshots/` folder.

If you want the reveal to feel snappier, the single knob is `powerRevealTime`; if you want bodies cleared further out of the lane, raise `powerRevealPush`.
