**Menu type** now uses a console-style system stack instead of the terminal monospace. [styles.css](styles.css) adds `--ui`:

`Bahnschrift` → `DIN Alternate` → `Avenir Next` → `Segoe UI Variable Text`/`Segoe UI` → `system-ui`

The body and the menu controls use it: main options, buttons, choices, arena/program cards, settings tabs, stage labels, notes, records, status lines, and the callsign field. The ASCII logo, boot log, room-code entry and schematic data tables stay on `--mono` so their columns keep their shape. On this Linux machine the named faces are not installed, so it resolves to the desktop `system-ui` font; Windows and macOS players get Bahnschrift or the DIN/Avenir fallback. The build is clean, but I did not do a browser screenshot pass on the new type.

**Atomize.exe** is also finished in this working tree. It has the white three-oval, six-segment hull with a vector atom core; alternating left/right electrons that arc and lightly seek; three persistent blue shield balls that each eat one hit or damage one contact; and a 2.8 s orbit field that captures shots, sentries and viruses, spins them by weight, lets Atomize keep walking, and throws everything outward on release. Bots use the kit, all numbers live under `ATOMIZE` in [programs.json](src/game/tuning/programs.json), and the implementation is in [world.ts](src/game/world.ts), [identity.ts](src/game/identity.ts), [render.ts](src/game/render.ts) and [programs.ts](src/game/programs.ts). [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) D25, [README.md](README.md), [TODO.md](TODO.md) and [HISTORY.md](HISTORY.md) are updated, and the build is stamped **0.1.49**.

**Checks:** `npm run build` passes (`tsc --noEmit` plus Vite). Headless `World` checks confirmed the ±239 launch angles at 480 speed, the seek turn, shield consumption, ball contact damage, gauntlet sentry and projectile capture, movement during the field, release impulses, and that captured homing missiles normalize to plain bolts so they cannot turn back on the caster. The temporary test script is removed. Everything is still uncommitted.

If you want to keep this from sitting uncommitted, the obvious next step is a scoped commit.
