Arena laser emitters are in, version `0.1.54`.

`CROSSROADS`, `THE RING`, and `MAINFRAME` now mount red wall fixtures, defined as arena data in [arenas.ts](src/game/arenas.ts). Each runs a 7-second cycle from [world.json](src/game/tuning/world.json): a 2.4-second gather where red dots and short streaks pull into the lens under a shrinking ring, a 0.42-second live beam, then rest. The two fixtures in each arena are offset half a cycle, so they alternate instead of firing together.

The beam uses the same surface test as the heavy laser, so pillars, deployed Wedge walls, the compactor plate and walled bounds stop the drawn shaft and the damage line together. A direct hit burns one health segment and shoves the body along the lane. The direct shaft only threatens players; the reflection is the offensive tool.

Raise the guard (`B`) while facing the lens to catch it. The return leaves along your facing rather than the heavy beam's fixed 37-degree glance, so holding target lock sends it at the locked enemy. It deals 2 damage over a longer reach, skips the guard so you cannot hit yourself, and can cut threats, the training drone, or another body.

The visuals include the wall bracket and lens, converging gather dots, layered red shaft, muzzle and impact flares, red side sparks, and emitter studs on the arena preview and minimap. Matches and VS BOTS build no fixtures at all, so the host and guests see the same arena, and nothing emitter-shaped enters `Snapshot` or `NetView`.

Placement also got checked: The Ring's first pass fired through its side gates, which are the spawn pair, and Mainframe's lanes sat on the y=720 spawn line. Both moved. A headless check now fails if a local start point sits inside an emitter lane. Bots do not path around the beams yet, so they can stand in one.

`npm run build` passes. Focused headless checks covered the gather timing, one burn per pass, the guard catch with no self-damage, the reflected 2-damage hit, match dormancy, every lane clearing its mount, and spawn clearance. In the running browser, CROSSROADS and THE RING reached live beams, the autoplay match reported zero emitters, and the console stayed clean after a full reload. Commits `c3e1c61` and `e7efda7` are pushed to `main`, and both GitHub Pages deploys succeeded. Probe's own heavy laser is unchanged; the emitters reuse its read.

The natural next step is making the bots treat the beams as real hazards, since they currently ignore them.
