The phone framework is in and deployed as **v0.1.57**.

**What was added**
- [src/ui/touch.ts](src/ui/touch.ts): a bottom-left analog stick and three hold-capable buttons at the bottom right. `SHIELD` maps to melee (`tap`) and guard/reflect (`hold`), `SKILL` maps to skill (`tap`) and power attack (`hold`), and `DASH` supports tap and charged dash. Everything writes ordinary `InputFrame` bits, so the simulation, guests and bots all see the same input path. Pointer release, pointer cancel, blur and a hidden tab clear every held control.
- [src/main.ts](src/main.ts): touch detection via a coarse pointer, with `?touch=1` / `?touch=0` QA overrides. Touch is only shown during a live local or guest game, not in menus, loading, the attract demo or the stress bench. The top-right pause control opens the normal leave overlay.
- **Settings > Controls**: persisted `AUTO LOCK` and `AUTO ATTACK`. Both default on for touch and off for keyboard/gamepad. Auto attack holds the normal target lock, fires ranged outside reach, and switches to melee inside `AUTO_ATTACK.meleeRange`; it never overrides a held shield/skill/dash, an active heavy or an armed jump-scare. The ranges live in [player.json](src/game/tuning/player.json).
- [src/game/render.ts](src/game/render.ts): the touch layout moves readiness docks to the top centre and suppresses the minimap. The stick and buttons use safe-area insets, and the controls sit above the canvas HUD but below overlays. `GAME UI` hides the canvas readout without taking away the phone's only controls.
- [index.html](index.html), [styles.css](styles.css): touch controls, the new settings tab, and a touch-specific How To Play table. [README.md](README.md), [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) (D28), [TODO.md](TODO.md) and [HISTORY.md](HISTORY.md) were updated.

**Verified**
- `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` pass.
- In the running build at 843×390: the stick moved the avatar and released to zero; the shield raised guard and released into cooldown; the pause button hid and restored the touch layer; auto-lock acquired a visible bot; auto-attack fired; `?touch=0` left both assists off; settings persisted across a reload.
- The production Pages build reports `v0.1.57`, shows the touch layer on `?touch=1`, and has no console errors.

Commit `da83ef8` is pushed, and the Pages deploy completed.

Production: <https://spuds0588.github.io/DEFLECT/?touch=1>

**Limitation:** this was verified with synthetic pointer events, not a physical phone. Portrait is usable but not laid out for it, and thumb reach/button placement still needs a real-device pass. Those are recorded as next items.

The natural next step is a real iPhone/Android pass to tune thumb reach and safe-area spacing.
