Worms now bite, viruses charge, and the small sentries ram. All three attacks are telegraphed, commit to a direction, respect cover, and have their own wind-up, active window, recovery, and cooldown.

- **Worms** bite when you are inside 76 units: 0.32 s rear-up, a 0.16 s lunge at 210 u/s into a 56-unit reach, 1 damage, an 880 shove, then recovery. The jaws open during the tell and snap shut on the lunge. Touch damage is suppressed for the whole attack.
- **Viruses** charge between 34 and 150 units: 0.34 s wind-up, a 0.22 s dash at 620, 1 damage, a 540 shove, then recovery. They still add infection on a hit.
- **Pulse squares and dart flocks** stop firing and ram a player inside 92 units: 0.3 s wind-up, a 0.16 s dash at 460, 1 damage, a 620 shove, then recovery. Only one sentry ram can commit at a time, so a flock cannot stack three hits on one frame. Triplex and homing silhouettes keep their shooting bands; cascading errors stay rooted.

The virus and sentry dashes share a dashed guide, arc, and arrow during the wind-up, then a hot streak on the dash. The worm uses teeth instead so it reads as a bite. Everything is tunable in [threats.json](src/game/tuning/threats.json) under `WORM.bite*`, `VIRUS.charge*`, and `SENTRY.ram`; the behaviour lives in [world.ts](src/game/world.ts) and the visuals in [render.ts](src/game/render.ts). [README.md](README.md), [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md), [TODO.md](TODO.md), and [HISTORY.md](HISTORY.md) are updated, and the build is stamped **v0.1.58**.

**Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` pass. A headless simulation confirmed the worm bite, virus charge, and sentry ram each start and deal exactly 1 damage, and that a second sentry at the same range stays out of the ram. I also loaded the wave-72 attract run in the browser through several restarts with no console errors. The Pages deploy completed successfully; production reports v0.1.58 at <https://spuds0588.github.io/DEFLECT/>.

Pushed as `89853de`, with a small note correction in `e227bc0`. **Limitation:** I have not played the tells by hand in a live wave 3+ run, so the exact timings and whether the 880 bite shove feels too strong still need a real pass.

The natural next step is a hands-on gauntlet pass at the waves where each threat first appears.
