- The anchored float loop is gone. The parent now moves on a slowly wandering heading (`floatTurn` 0.32, `floatTurnRate` 1.15 rad/s) at 44 u/s, eased in and out so it never snaps.
- It keeps a loose band around the player (`floatRing` 250): past 1.35x it turns its heading back toward the fight, inside 0.6x it turns away. Turning the heading rather than adding an opposing vector matters — two canceling vectors just parked the body at the band edge.
- It reflects its heading off an inset border (`floatMargin` 130) before the bounds clamp catches it, so it floats around the room instead of grinding along a wall. Cover still pushes it out as before.
- The triangle reuses the parked sentry `orbitA`/`orbitR`/`orbitDir` fields (heading, home radius, turn sign), seeded per subject at spawn. No snapshot or protocol fields were added; calibration stays local.
